 | SEC-15 | low | **Room transcripts are not framed as data** (wave 42). A member's turn prompt lists the room's recent messages as `who: text` lines, other members' replies included, unfenced; a reply holding a newline can forge a line in the person's name, and a member that read outside text can pass it on. Members are the owner's own profiles; tools still run under each member's approvals. | **open**, follow-up: fence members' messages (`core.untrusted`) and escape line starts in the transcript; together with approvals in room turns (wave-42 follow-up) | `tests/unit/gateway/rooms/test_loop.py` |
