+| SEC-17 | high | **certifi 2026.7.22 trusts the emSign roots** (GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2, rated critical; SEC2-2). Fixed in 2026.10.19, uploaded after uv `exclude-newer` and inside the 14-day age rule. aiohttp 3.14.3 (slack extra, client only) and vite 8.3.2 (dev only) carried high advisories (SEC2-3, SEC2-4): **fixed** by the wave 46 re-lock (aiohttp 3.14.4, vite 8.3.3; pynacl 1.6.2 for its moderate one; `exclude-newer` 2026-10-08). | certifi **allow-listed** with a dated reason to 2026-11-08 (the aiohttp and vite entries were dropped in wave 46); the entry expires on purpose, so `deps_audit` fails from 2026-11-09 until the lead moves `exclude-newer` past 2026-10-20 (or grants a dated exception) and re-locks certifi | `tooling/checks/tests/test_deps_audit.py` |
 | SEC-18 | info | **SEC2 observations** (no data leaves today): `IpcRegistry.seal()` answers an unregistered sync channel without the sender check; gated mode lets an unsafe request with no `Origin` past the CSRF check (non-browser clients; `SameSite=Lax` cookies); `cookies.read` also accepts the unprefixed cookie name on https; the SPA has no script CSP (one inline bootstrap). | **open**, follow-ups (small): sender-check every sync channel, prefer the `__Host-` name on https, hash-based `script-src` | `apps/desktop/electron/security/audit.test.ts` |
 
